  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A black and white screen print styled as a vintage advertisement for an Immobilization Chamber, with a man in glasses beside a diagram of a body in a frame, and a brain logo reading Instruments for Psychological Testing.",
    "description": "A portrait format screen print in black ink on white paper. Bold condensed headline type reads Immobilization Chamber across the top, with DAYS WEEKS MONTHS YEARS stacked at upper right. A high contrast halftone image shows a man with short hair and glasses looking down beside a tall framed apparatus containing a silhouette of a standing human body with a helmet like fixture over the head. Vertical text along the left edge reads Effect of severe immobilization of the body on intellectual and perceptual process. A circular seal at lower right shows a brain with roots like a tree and the words Instruments for Psychological Testing. A box at the bottom reads Zubeck et al, 1963.",
    "impression": "A fake product catalogue page for an apparatus from a real and unsettling line of sensory deprivation research. The deadpan commercial layout, the seal and the citation turn a historical experiment into a parody advertisement. It is funny and chilling in equal measure, and very much a cognitive psychologist's joke.",
